From 96555f2d59274b8149ef2b7a072a20d142706fe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abtraore <abdrahtraore97@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:55:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] saturn: decode launch reductions for Qwen3.5 ternary
 (Bonsai 27B)

- relax the gate/up/GLU fusion memory check on the quantized matvec path: the kernel reads a private q8_1 copy of
  src1, so a GLU output placed on src1's memory is harmless. 24 of 64 ffn layers were refused before (default on,
  GGML_CUDA_FUSE_GLU_RELAXED=0 to disable)
- dual-output matvec: two batch-1 MUL_MATs on the same input with same-shape weights run as one launch (ssm_alpha +
  ssm_beta, attn_k + attn_v). mmvf and mmvq epilogues write the second result to fusion.dst2 (default on,
  GGML_CUDA_FUSE_DUAL_MATVEC=0 to disable)
- per-graph q8_1 activation cache in a persistent arena, keyed on the view root (opt-in GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_SHARE_Q8=1)
- experiment switches for the PQ2_0 block geometry (GGML_CUDA_PQ2_WIDE, GGML_CUDA_PQ2_SMALLK): flat on sm120
- launch statistics name unfused GLU nodes and report q8 cache hits

Decode graph 1542 -> 1430 launches, 7.22 -> 7.08 ms/token on one RTX 5090, output identical (sha e3edc1330e4f).
